# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This repo tracks the SCRIPTS only - never the photos.
#
# The library can be 100+ GB. Git would try to store every byte, forever, and
# would be a catastrophic way to back up photos. Your actual backup is the
# BackupPath mirror in config.json plus an external/offsite copy.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The photo library itself
Library/
Groups/
.staging/

# Derived state: rebuildable, and large (catalog.jsonl is ~10 MB at 20k photos)
state/
logs/

# Third-party binary, fetched separately (see README)
tools/

# config.json IS tracked - it holds no secrets, just your paths and options,
# and having it versioned means you can undo a bad settings change.

# Windows noise
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*.lnk
